From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: one VMA block size for the default blocks and the separate pools (lethevimlet, oot-bc250 9cc177c + c8594b8), off by default

Switch: EDEN_UP_VMA_BLOCK_MIB=<n> (digits only, 2 to 64, read once). Unset, or anything else (1, 65,
"8x", " 8", empty): exactly T146, with a warning line for a set but refused value.

What: VMA takes device memory from the driver in blocks and places allocations inside them;
anything over half a block gets memory of its own. Today our default blocks (images) are 16 MiB or
EDEN_VMA_BLOCK_MIB's size (0158, 2 to 64), while the separate pools (sparse pages and the buffer
cache's buffers, Device::SeparatePool) stay at a fixed 16 MiB, and their half-block rule with them.
lethevimlet's EDEN_NX2_VMA_BLOCK_MIB sets one size for all of them. EDEN_UP_VMA_BLOCK_MIB does the
same here: n MiB for the default blocks (it wins over EDEN_VMA_BLOCK_MIB, the start line says so),
for the SparsePages and DeviceBuffers pools, for the over-half-a-block rules of
AllocateSparseMemory and CreateBufferInSeparatePool, and for 0521's TrimDefaultHalfBlock. 0521's own
trim blocks (EDEN_UP_VMA_TRIM_BLOCK_MIB) keep their own size. A start line names the size:
"EDEN_UP_VMA_BLOCK_MIB: n MiB device memory blocks (default blocks and separate pools; over n/2 MiB:
memory of its own)".

His numbers (BC-250, the same chip family and RADV driver, a later town): free space inside pooled
blocks 464 -> 22 MiB, device memory at the peak 5453 -> 5056 MiB, fps 54.4 -> 55.0 at 8 MiB; 4 MiB
saved nothing more and was slower. His c8594b8 also makes 8 the default; that half is NOT taken:
another tester's base-PS5 A/B (sbihaiko) gave 20-25 fps at 8 MiB against 60 at 16 (he called it
noise or worse), and run275 (T59) with EDEN_VMA_BLOCK_MIB=8 (default blocks only) still showed
333-389 MiB slack in its heavy scenes (0521's header, which names slack in the DeviceBuffers and
SparsePages pools as the next step: this is it). So this is a switch for an A/B on memory slack
("vma_slack" in EDEN_MEM_CENSUS_TOP was 265 MiB in the 13 Nov crash logs) and fps, not a default.

Cost when off: one function-local static read per separate-pool allocation and per pool creation
(the old constant), nothing else. Not in the shader-prep TranslationSwitches: it changes no
translation, so both arms keep one store. Risk when on: more blocks and more allocations of their
own (each two system calls), and a dedicated image of 2 MiB or more starts on a 2 MiB boundary in
the PS5 driver, so smaller blocks can move holes rather than remove them (0158's note).

Origin and credit: lethevimlet, lethevimlet/oot-bc250 (and lichii-bc250) v7, commits 9cc177c
(the switch) and c8594b8 (his 8 MiB default, not taken). Our switch name and range are ours.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_device.cpp b/src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_device.cpp
index 31d08b6..0e2799f 100644
--- a/src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_device.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/vulkan_common/vulkan_device.cpp
@@ -817,6 +817,18 @@ Device::Device(VkInstance instance_, vk::PhysicalDevice physical_, VkSurfaceKHR
             vma_block_bytes = VkDeviceSize{mib} << 20;
         }
     }
+    // EDEN_UP_VMA_BLOCK_MIB (0656): the default blocks and the separate pools together.
+    if (const VkDeviceSize up_block_bytes = UpVmaBlockBytes(); up_block_bytes != 0) {
+        vma_block_bytes = up_block_bytes;
+        LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan,
+                 "EDEN_UP_VMA_BLOCK_MIB: {} MiB device memory blocks (default blocks and separate "
+                 "pools; over {} MiB: memory of its own){}",
+                 up_block_bytes >> 20, up_block_bytes >> 21,
+                 std::getenv("EDEN_VMA_BLOCK_MIB") != nullptr ? ", EDEN_VMA_BLOCK_MIB ignored" : "");
+    } else if (const char* const up_value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_VMA_BLOCK_MIB")) {
+        LOG_WARNING(Render_Vulkan, "EDEN_UP_VMA_BLOCK_MIB={} ignored (digits only, 2 to 64)",
+                    up_value);
+    }
     // EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_CHURN=1 (Fritchii dcbd696438): counts the allocator's vkAllocateMemory /
     // vkFreeMemory calls (blocks and dedicated memory) for the "Churn (600 frames)" line.
     static const VmaDeviceMemoryCallbacks churn_callbacks{
@@ -896,6 +908,32 @@ Device::~Device() {
     vmaDestroyAllocator(allocator);
 }
 
+VkDeviceSize Device::UpVmaBlockBytes() {
+    static const VkDeviceSize bytes = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_VMA_BLOCK_MIB");
+        if (value == nullptr || value[0] == '\0') {
+            return VkDeviceSize{0};
+        }
+        u64 mib = 0;
+        for (const char* digit = value; *digit != '\0'; ++digit) {
+            if (*digit < '0' || *digit > '9' || mib > 64) {
+                return VkDeviceSize{0};
+            }
+            mib = mib * 10 + static_cast<u64>(*digit - '0');
+        }
+        return mib >= 2 && mib <= 64 ? VkDeviceSize{mib} << 20 : VkDeviceSize{0};
+    }();
+    return bytes;
+}
+
+VkDeviceSize Device::SeparatePoolBlockSize() {
+    static const VkDeviceSize bytes = [] {
+        const VkDeviceSize up = UpVmaBlockBytes();
+        return up != 0 ? up : VkDeviceSize{16} << 20;
+    }();
+    return bytes;
+}
+
 VmaPool Device::GetSeparatePool(SeparatePool kind, u32 memory_type,
                                 VkDeviceSize block_size) const {
     std::scoped_lock lk{separate_pools_mutex};
